      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَاعِثٌ</span></b>  [act. part. n. of 1; <i>Sending:</i> &amp;c. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And
hence, <i>Occasioning,</i> or <i>causing: an occasion,</i> or
<i>a cause;</i> and <i>a motive</i>]. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">البَاعِثُ</span> one of the names
[or epithets] of God; <i>The Quickener of mankind
after death, on the day of resurrection.</i> (TA.)

